 "derivation": "salineShare = saline_ha / total_ha of the upazila; classShares = class area / saline area; repECe = area-weighted class midpoint over the saline area (S5 uses its 16.0 dS/m lower bound). District values are area-weighted over that district's SRDI upazilas. All derived from SRDI 2010 Appendix-2 class areas.",
 "sourceNotes": [
  "SRDI 2010 p.1: 'Most of the land remains fallow in the dry season (January-May) because of soil salinity, lack of good quality irrigation water and late draining condition.'",
  "SRDI 2010 p.2: the field survey ran in May 2009, 2500 soil samples along 3-4 km traverses; EC was measured on a 1:5 soil-water extract.",
  "SRDI 2010 p.8: 'most of the vegetable crops are said to be very sensitive to saline condition and their yield decreased from 6-19% with each unit increase in salinity' - the same order as the Maas-Hoffman slopes used here."
 ],
 "areaNote": "37 of the SRDI rows print a total area that is not cultivated+uncultivated (hill, forest reserve and char land sit inside the administrative total; five rows that Appendix-1 marks with an asterisk print the opposite way). salineShare divides by the printed total, so on those rows it is a lower bound; agricultural_ha is published with every value.",
